finding: Trace consumption can fail open: moduleResolutions returns a partial or empty map without checking completeness, and checkImports silently continues when a scanned import has no map entry. A successful tsc whose trace format or output stream changes can therefore drop reds. The fixture uses real tsc and asserts its planted self-name, .js, alias and file-kind imports, so a total parser break or a missing mapping for those cases would fail it; missing mappings elsewhere are not covered. Scratch proof: with tsconfig including only src/extras, the scanned src/core/rendering/index.ts standard-to-extras violation returns no reds because tsc never traced that importer. Compiler errors do fail loudly via the nonzero check. Also bun test scripts/check-imports.test.ts currently fails: its real tsc child exceeds the 250ms unit budget (~254ms) and is killed, so the required fixture test does not pass. No files changed.
